# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev` (npm run preview).
# These are WORKER RUNTIME secrets, read per request by the SSR routes through
# `cloudflare:workers`. They are NOT the same thing as the build-time variables
# in `.env`, and Astro's dev server does not read this file.
#
# In production set them with:
#   npx wrangler secret put SANITY_TOKEN

# ── Live draft preview (/preview/**, /api/draft-mode/*) ──────────────────────
# A Sanity token with read access to DRAFTS. Viewer permission is enough.
# Create it at sanity.io/manage -> your project -> API -> Tokens.
#
# Everything FAILS CLOSED without it: /api/draft-mode/enable cannot mint a valid
# preview cookie (the fingerprint is empty, so no cookie can ever match),
# /preview/live refuses the connection, and the preview routes error rather than
# quietly serving published content dressed up as a draft. A fresh clone with no
# token still builds and still serves the public site; only the preview is off.
#
# One more setup step lives outside this repo: the embedded Studio has to be
# allowed to talk to the Sanity API from your origin.
#   npx sanity cors add http://localhost:4321 --credentials
#   npx sanity cors add https://<your-worker>.workers.dev --credentials
SANITY_TOKEN=

# ── Writing help in the Studio (/api/studio/ai/, PORTS.md card 123) ─────────
# A Claude API key from console.anthropic.com. Optional: without it the Studio's
# "Suggest" buttons do not appear. In production:
#   npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Google Analytics 4 and Search Console on Home (PORTS.md card 136) ───────
# The studio's sites read Google through studio-status (the SITE_DATA service
# binding and the SITE_DATA_KEY var in wrangler.jsonc), so they need nothing
# here. A local `wrangler dev` reaches studio-status only when it also runs
# locally. OPTIONAL FALLBACK for a site outside the studio's account: its own
# service-account JSON key, whole, on ONE line, plus the plain settings
#   GA4_PROPERTY_ID      the numeric property id, not the G- measurement id
#   SEARCH_CONSOLE_SITE  sc-domain:example.com or https://example.com/
# In production: npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT
# ANALYTICS_PROVIDER: cloudflare or ga4 (unset: whichever is set up, Cloudflare first).
# Setup: docs/agent/studio-kit.md, "Google Analytics and Search Console".
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
GA4_PROPERTY_ID=
SEARCH_CONSOLE_SITE=
ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=
